      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): honor empty document extractor scope",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nDocument extractor resolution treated an explicit empty plugin scope as if no scope was provided. With `onlyPluginIds: []`, document extractor discovery could still expand bundled extractor owners instead of returning no extractors.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe plugin scope helper already preserves the difference between an omitted scope and an explicitly empty scope. This change moves the fix to the shared bundled manifest contract resolver and uses the same helper for the document extractor allowlist branch, so both bundled contract discovery and document extractor resolution share one scope contract.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCallers that intentionally pass an empty document extractor scope now get no extractors, including when an operator plugin allowlist is present. Omitted scope still discovers enabled bundled document extractors normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Changed `src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.ts` to use `createPluginIdScopeSet` instead of a local helper that collapsed empty scopes.\n- Changed `src/plugins/document-extractors.runtime.ts` to use the same scope helper for the operator allowlist branch.\n- Added `src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.test.ts` proving omitted scope still returns a bundled contract owner while `onlyPluginIds: []` returns none.\n- Kept document extractor regression coverage for empty scope with and without an operator allowlist.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.test.ts src/plugins/document-extractors.runtime.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose` passed: 2 files / 6 tests.\n- `corepack pnpm format:check src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.ts src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.test.ts src/plugins/document-extractors.runtime.ts src/plugins/document-extractors.runtime.test.ts` passed.\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.ts src/plugins/bundled-manifest-contract-plugins.test.ts src/plugins/document-extractors.runtime.ts src/plugins/document-extractors.runtime.test.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD` and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Controlled runtime proof: `node --import tsx - <<'EOF' ...` invoked the real document extractor resolver without test mocks.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Controlled runtime proof with omitted scope returned the real bundled extractor owner: `unscopedCount: 1`, sample `{ id: \"pdf\", pluginId: \"document-extract\", mimeTypes: [\"application/pdf\"] }`.\n- Controlled runtime proof with `onlyPluginIds: []` returned no extractors: `emptyScopeCount: 0`, `emptyScope: []`.\n- Controlled runtime proof with an operator allowlist plus `onlyPluginIds: []` also returned no extractors: `allowedEmptyScopeCount: 0`, `allowedEmptyScope: []`.\n- The branch was refreshed onto current main after the fix commit.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/document-extractor-empty-allowlist",
        "head_sha": "daf0137783ac48746bd5cf919ca71d8d535f4408",
